<rml>
<head>
	<title>Folio view model test</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="/folio/folio.rcss"/>
	<style>
		body { background-color: #14141ae8; color: #e8e8f0; font-size: 17dp; padding: 16dp;
		       width: 100%; height: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; }
		h2 { font-size: 13dp; color: #8a8a99; margin-bottom: 8dp; }
		p { margin-bottom: 5dp; }
		.v { color: #f0c674; }
		.bar { width: 300dp; height: 14dp; background-color: #2b2b36; border-radius: 3dp;
		       margin: 4dp 0 12dp 0; }
		.fill { height: 14dp; background-color: #4ec9a0; border-radius: 3dp; }
		.down .fill { background-color: #e06c75; }
		.note { color: #8a8a99; font-size: 13dp; margin-top: 12dp; }
		.row { display: flex; margin: 4dp 0 8dp 0; }
		.lbl { width: 90dp; color: #8a8a99; font-size: 15dp; }
		input[type="range"] { width: 200dp; height: 16dp; margin-right: 10dp; nav: auto; }
		input[type="range"] sliderbar { width: 12dp; height: 16dp; background-color: #8a8a99;
		                                border-radius: 2dp; }
		input[type="range"] slidertrack { height: 4dp; margin-top: 6dp; background-color: #2b2b36; }
		input[type="range"]:focus-visible sliderbar { background-color: #4ec9a0; }
		input[type="checkbox"] { width: 16dp; height: 16dp; background-color: #2b2b36;
		                         border-radius: 2dp; margin-right: 10dp; nav: auto; }
		input[type="checkbox"]:checked { background-color: #4ec9a0; }
		input[type="checkbox"]:focus-visible { border: 1dp #e8e8f0; }
		input[type="text"] { width: 160dp; padding: 3dp 6dp; margin-right: 10dp; nav: auto;
		                     background-color: #2b2b36; color: #e8e8f0; border-radius: 2dp; }
		input[type="text"]:focus-visible { border: 1dp #4ec9a0; }
		button { padding: 6dp 14dp; margin-right: 8dp; border-radius: 3dp;
		         background-color: #2b2b36; color: #e8e8f0; font-size: 15dp; nav: auto; }
		button:hover { background-color: #3a3a48; }
		button:focus-visible { background-color: #4ec9a0; color: #14141a; }
	</style>
</head>
<body data-model="test">
	<h2>bound off a UObject that reports its own field changes</h2>
	<p>Ticks <span class="v">{{ Ticks }}</span></p>
	<p>Health <span class="v">{{ Health }}</span></p>
	<p>bAlive <span class="v">{{ bAlive }}</span></p>
	<p>Status <span class="v">{{ Status }}</span></p>

	<h2>the same value driving a style</h2>
	<div class="bar" data-class-down="!bAlive">
		<div class="fill" data-style-width="Health * 300 + 'dp'"></div>
	</div>

	<h2>commands: markup calling back into the UObject</h2>
	<div class="row">
		<button data-event-click="ToggleDrift">{{ bDrifting ? 'Hold Health' : 'Resume drift' }}</button>
		<button data-event-click="Revive">Revive</button>
		<button data-event-click="Damage(0.25, 'a button')">Damage(0.25)</button>
		<button data-event-click="Damage(0.6, 'the other button')">Damage(0.6)</button>
	</div>
	<p class="note">These are UFUNCTION(BlueprintCallable) on the source, bound by reflection like the
	properties. Health and Status must move, and the log names the call and its arguments. CountCommands
	returns a value, so the bridge must refuse it: the warning naming it is the pass. Hold Health first,
	or the drift makes the other two impossible to read.</p>

	<h2>two-way: a control writing back through the property</h2>
	<div class="row">
		<span class="lbl">Volume</span>
		<input type="range" min="0" max="100" step="1" id="w_volume" data-value="Volume"/>
		<span class="v">{{ Volume }}</span>
	</div>
	<div class="row">
		<span class="lbl">Gamma</span>
		<input type="range" min="0.5" max="2.5" step="0.1" id="w_gamma" data-value="Gamma"/>
		<span class="v">{{ format(Gamma, 2) }}</span>
	</div>
	<div class="row">
		<span class="lbl">Subtitles</span>
		<input type="checkbox" id="w_subs" data-checked="bSubtitles"/>
		<span class="v">{{ bSubtitles }}</span>
	</div>
	<div class="row">
		<span class="lbl">Name</span>
		<input type="text" id="w_name" data-value="PlayerName" size="16"/>
		<span class="v">{{ PlayerName }}</span>
	</div>
	<p class="note">The number beside each control is a second binding to the same property, so it only
	tracks if the write reached the object and announced itself. A value that moves and springs back
	means the write stopped at the mirror.</p>
	<div class="row">
		<span class="lbl">Health</span>
		<input type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.05" id="w_health" data-value="Health"/>
		<span class="v">{{ format(Health, 2) }}</span>
	</div>
	<p class="note">Health is BlueprintReadOnly, so this slider must refuse to move it and the log must
	say why once. That is the other half of the test.</p>

	<p class="note">Hidden is a UPROPERTY with no BlueprintReadOnly or EditAnywhere, so it must not be
	bound. Staying as literal braces is the pass, and the "could not add data-text view" warnings that
	go with it are expected here: <span class="v">{{ Hidden }}</span></p>
	<p class="note">The source implements INotifyFieldValueChanged, the same interface
	UMVVMViewModelBase does, so these update by notification rather than polling. The log says which:
	look for "updating by notification".</p>
	<p class="note">folio.MvvmTest off to close.</p>
</body>
</rml>
